# Craton UI/UX Direction

## Brand feel

- Innovation-first, research-led, evidence-heavy trust.
- Visual language may evolve beyond the old ink/paper/copper/sage system — keep it **premium, calm, technical**, never generic SaaS purple or template-looking.
- Atmosphere > flat fills; real product surfaces > empty decoration.
- Motion must **inform or delight with purpose**; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Pause heavy animation off-screen.

## Hero (highest priority)

- Poetic line may stay as kicker (“Bold ideas. Engineered forward.”).
- **H1 or primary subhead must say the job + audience** (e.g. AI for EU MDR/IVDR technical documentation / GSPR gap assessment).
- Show a **product visual early** (GSPR mock or compact UI), not only abstract canvas art.
- Primary CTA: **Request a pilot** / **Book a demo** in header + hero (not vague “Explore”).
- Avoid clutter that competes with CTA (phase sculpture controls are optional / simplify).

## Page craft

- One clear job per section; generous hierarchy; supporting text ≥12–13px; labels ≥11px; WCAG AA contrast.
- Show **both products** without forcing a second tab click (cards side-by-side, then expand).
- Proof once, loud (patents, enterprise evaluation) — do not spam the same metric everywhere.
- Nav labels: `RAccelerator`, `ReviewsIntel`, `How it works`, `About`, `Contact`.
- Mobile-first: stress-test 360–390px for header, product table, hero CTAs.

## Creativity license

- Invent distinctive layouts, transitions, and micro-interactions that feel human and market-leading.
- Do not ship a clone of Greenlight Guru / Qualio, and do not ship a clone of the old HTML — **outperform both on clarity and craft**.
